# Puerto BJJ Project Rules

## Technology Stack
- Rails 8.0.2 with no-build approach (propshaft, importmap)
- CSS-Zero (Laxaro Nixon) - NOT Tailwind CSS
- Kamal 2.5.6 for deployment
- Hetzner hosting (webhosting + server)
- Stimulus for JavaScript interactions
- Lucide Rails for icons
- SQLite (dev) (prod)

## CSS Guidelines
- Use CSS-Zero variables: --color-bg, --color-text, --color-primary, --color-text-reversed
- NEVER use Tailwind classes or utilities
- Follow existing patterns in shared/header.css
- Fix dark mode CSS variables in base.css (currently broken)
- Mobile-first responsive design
- Use CSS custom properties for theming

## JavaScript Guidelines
- Use Stimulus controllers for all interactivity
- Follow existing patterns in app/javascript/controllers/
- Maintain sticky header functionality (works on mobile, issues on desktop)
- Clean up event listeners in disconnect() methods

## Deployment Guidelines
- Use Kamal 2.5.6 for deployment orchestration
- Configure KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD in .kamal/secrets (currently has circular reference)
- Use Docker Hub registry (daniel01ariasjaen/puerto-bjj)
- Follow Hetzner hosting patterns
- Test deployment with --verbose flag if issues arise

## File Structure Conventions
- CSS variables: app/assets/stylesheets/css-zero/base.css
- Header styles: app/assets/stylesheets/shared/header.css
- Deploy config: config/deploy.yml
- Secrets: .kamal/secrets
- Stimulus controllers: app/javascript/controllers/
- Shared views: app/views/shared/

## Known Issues to Address
- Dark mode CSS variables incorrectly configured in base.css
- Deploy requires proper KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD setup
- White text appears on white background in some browsers/devices
- Circular reference in .kamal/secrets file

## Code Quality Standards
- Use RuboCop for Ruby code formatting
- Use Brakeman for security analysis
- Follow Rails conventions for naming and structure
- Write descriptive commit messages
- Test on both mobile and desktop before deploying

## Performance Considerations
- Optimize images for web delivery
- Use CSS transforms for animations (better performance)
- Minimize JavaScript bundle size
- Use passive event listeners where appropriate
- Implement proper caching strategies

## Security Guidelines
- Never commit secrets or sensitive data
- Use environment variables for configuration
- Validate all user inputs
- Follow Rails security best practices
- Keep dependencies updated

## Testing Requirements
- Test sticky header on mobile and desktop
- Verify CSS variables work in light and dark modes
- Test deployment process before production
- Validate responsive design across devices
- Check for text contrast issues

## Git Workflow
- Use feature branches for new development
- Test in staging environment before production
- Write descriptive commit messages
- Keep commits atomic and focused
- Use pull requests for code review 